We introduce a one-parameter family of Jordanian twists for the quantum group $U_q(\mathfrak{sl}_2)$, which generalizes the standard Jordanian twist. This family is constructed using the $q$-deformed exponential function. We demonstrate that this twist is compatible with the $q$-deformed Weyl algebra and the $q$-deformed Heisenberg algebra. Furthermore, we establish that the twist is nontrivial for all values of the parameter. Finally, we derive the corresponding $R$-matrix and the associated braided Hopf algebra.
